WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:03.730
I'm so happy to talk to
you, Patton, God bless you.

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:05.800
Yeah, that's just, trust me,

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:08.490
this interview has been a lifeline for me,

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:10.670
this has been like
holding concert tickets.

00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:12.517
I've known about it for a
couple of weeks and it's like,

00:00:12.517 --> 00:00:14.894
"If I can just get to Tuesday
morning and talk to Conan."

00:00:14.894 --> 00:00:17.800
(both laugh)

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:19.150
This is, no, seriously,

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:22.100
I was coming to the
theater today to tape this

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:25.800
and I was thinking, "Oh
great, I'm so starved

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:27.610
to talk to funny people,"

00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:29.030
and you're one of my favorite people,

00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:30.690
and I was like, "I get
to talk to Patton today."

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:33.330
And so I think I drove 80 miles an hour

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:36.830
to get to the theater, just
so we can have this interview.

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:39.220
Let's make this about you
and then more about me.

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:40.380
Yes.

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:42.150
How are you doing during isolation?

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:43.500
Are you handling this all right?

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:47.162
And why are you sitting in
a Loews Theater right now?

00:00:47.162 --> 00:00:47.995
(chuckles) Look,

00:00:47.995 --> 00:00:49.653
when the shelter-in-place order came down,

00:00:50.781 --> 00:00:53.309
I was in the early
screening of "Black Widow".

00:00:53.309 --> 00:00:55.280
(Conan laughs)
No spoilers, like you know,

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:56.260
I'm just, I've been in place

00:00:56.260 --> 00:00:58.970
and you can live on Red Vines and Sprite.

00:00:58.970 --> 00:01:03.550
People don't understand this,
but it's a very intense diet.

00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:07.630
So you'd been saying that
they shouted COVID quarantine

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:09.070
while the movie was ending,

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:11.030
and you just said, "I'll just stay here."

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:12.240
I go, "Yeah," I was,

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:13.660
at well, first I thought is this part,

00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:16.100
is this the next phase
of the Marvel movies

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:19.210
where they actually add some
kinda outside threatening?

00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:20.190
Oh no, it's really real,

00:01:20.190 --> 00:01:22.560
and I'm kind of the last one left here,

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:24.630
a lot of us have gone insane.

00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:25.770
There's one other guy,

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:27.480
but he's living under the seats now.

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:29.974
So it's just, I'm kind
of the spokesman, it's...

00:01:29.974 --> 00:01:32.580
(Conan laughs)

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:34.776
They said you, you will
speak for all of us here

00:01:34.776 --> 00:01:36.630
at the abandoned theater.

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:39.350
I mean, I've been handling things okay.

00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:42.510
I realized the other day that
a lot of times in the morning

00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:44.730
I will go sit on my front porch.

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:47.190
We have like a front porch swing,

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:48.710
and I'll sit out there and read a book

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:51.700
and the same people will go walking by

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:53.550
and I'm starting to worry

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:57.350
that I'm becoming the weird
fixture in the neighborhood.

00:01:57.350 --> 00:02:00.930
The guy in his robe and cargo shorts

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:02.830
just kinda waving at people with a book

00:02:02.830 --> 00:02:04.890
and they use me as a, "Oh it's,

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:06.870
well, it's 9:00 a.m, he's out there."

00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:10.007
Like I'm the weird
neighborhood clock now to tape

00:02:10.007 --> 00:02:13.710
and to step things by,
but I've become a guy

00:02:13.710 --> 00:02:16.160
who sits on his front
porch and waves at people.

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:17.250
Right, right, yes.

00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:19.410
The thing you as a child or as a teenager,

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:21.650
you thought I'll never be that guy, ever.

00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:25.540
Yes, that, oh my God,
I'm the guy, no I am,

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:28.310
I'm the guy in slasher
movie at the beginning

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:30.920
who's like, "That house
has a death curse."

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:32.869
And like, "Shut up. (mumbles)"
(Conan laughs)

00:02:32.869 --> 00:02:36.780
Like I'm, oh god, I turned into that guy.

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:38.185
Yes, you're that guy,

00:02:38.185 --> 00:02:40.947
"Oh, you don't wanna go
up there, I tell ya."

00:02:40.947 --> 00:02:43.400
"Don't go to the old beards lay place,

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:46.248
it's a murder house,"
and they're, "Shut up."

00:02:46.248 --> 00:02:48.360
(chuckles) You know what I'm missing now,

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:50.070
a hair and makeup team.

00:02:50.070 --> 00:02:52.800
I am missing a hair and makeup team.

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:56.850
When, okay, first off your
hair, they should take,

00:02:56.850 --> 00:02:58.840
they should use time-lapse
photos, that should be

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:01.940
the chronicle of this
quarantine, it's Conan's hair.

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:05.270
The ongoing, like the, the
bigger and bigger it gets.

00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:07.820
When this quarantine ends,

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:10.140
every actor and actress,
we should organize

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:14.260
some massive dinner celebration parade

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:15.890
just for hair and makeup people.

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:18.630
They should be, whenever we see them,

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:20.837
we should like avert our gaze and kneel.

00:03:20.837 --> 00:03:22.150
Yes, yes.

00:03:22.150 --> 00:03:25.990
They are so clearly such a crucial,

00:03:25.990 --> 00:03:28.520
they're beyond crucial in show business.

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:32.270
I mean, we knew that they
were valuable, but my God,

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:36.390
the next, whatever the next
live Academy Award should be,

00:03:36.390 --> 00:03:39.340
there should be, they should like have a,

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:41.370
they should like bring a
powder puff out on stage,

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:43.790
we should all like stand
and just kind of worship it.

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:44.662
Just like
(Conan laughs)

00:03:44.662 --> 00:03:47.123
bow our heads down and (mumbles)

00:03:47.123 --> 00:03:49.460
some kind of this shining thing.

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:50.740
Right.
Oh my God,

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:52.020
hair and makeup people,

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:54.060
I've always tried to be nice to you,

00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:55.570
but I was not being nice enough.

00:03:55.570 --> 00:03:57.256
I promise you, this is,

00:03:57.256 --> 00:03:59.750
I'm gonna show up in
that trailer every day

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:03.440
with muffins and coffee
and just, thank you.

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:05.710
No, I've been frightening people online

00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:07.950
with my hair everyday on the show,

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:10.310
because every day, like some days

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:11.840
I kinda comb it up a little bit,

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:13.330
but it's gotten so long.

00:04:13.330 --> 00:04:14.330
[Patton] Jesus.

00:04:14.330 --> 00:04:16.560
There's like nine feet of hair

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:19.280
and then it turns into this tsunami.

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:21.710
But then if I let it go, it comes down

00:04:21.710 --> 00:04:23.093
and I sort of look like,

00:04:24.007 --> 00:04:27.650
"Hey man, I'm just playing my song, man."

00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:29.320
And I'm pushing my hair back this way

00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:33.410
and yeah, it's, but I'm
just sort of enjoying

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:37.080
letting it all go, just let it all go.

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:39.020
Yeah, if you didn't have any product

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:39.930
in your hair right now,

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:42.520
you would look like the
one viking on the raid

00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:44.230
that like knows what all the,

00:04:44.230 --> 00:04:45.840
like the codes and codexes mean,

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:47.617
like there's the big
brawny guys who are like,

00:04:47.617 --> 00:04:49.450
"No, this means there'd be dragons,"

00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:51.370
listen to like, you're
the guy they bring along-

00:04:51.370 --> 00:04:52.640
Wait a minute, so I'm not

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:55.860
the good fighter or the strong Viking.

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:59.070
I'm the guy that's like,
"I know the signs."

00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:01.579
Well, no, they bring
you along to translate

00:05:01.579 --> 00:05:03.930
like so they make sure they
don't open any cursed items,

00:05:03.930 --> 00:05:06.420
that's who they bring on.
[Conan] Thanks a lot.

